<title>UK: One Brent cargo kept, second in dispute.</title>
<headline>One Brent cargo kept, second in dispute.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of two Brent cargoes due to turn wet on Wednesday was kept ahead of the five o'clock deadline, traders said.</p>
<p>The cargo, due to load Sept 10-12, was kept by British Petroleum.</p>
<p>The other cargo was being disputed by U.S. major Chevron and Wall Street trader Morgan Stanley, traders said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
